{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_comment": [
    "Engineering framework permissions floor. Copy the `permissions` object",
    "into your repository's .claude/settings.json, or let",
    "/engineering-framework:framework-install merge it for you.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS A FILE YOU COPY RATHER THAN SOMETHING THE PLUGIN SHIPS:",
    "a plugin's settings.json supports only the `agent` and",
    "`subagentStatusLine` keys, so a plugin cannot ship permission rules. The",
    "plugin's command guard hook covers the same operations and more forms, but",
    "a hook is executable code that can fail, and Claude Code treats a crashed",
    "hook as a non-blocking error. A deny rule cannot fail open. Install both.",
    "",
    "Every Bash rule is mirrored as a PowerShell rule. The PowerShell tool is",
    "enabled by default on Windows without Git Bash and Bash(...) rules do not",
    "govern it, so an unmirrored floor silently disappears on those machines.",
    "",
    "File rules are only consulted for the Read and Edit tools. A Write(...),",
    "Glob(...), MultiEdit(...) or NotebookEdit(...) path rule is accepted,",
    "never consulted, and warns at startup - the worst failure shape available,",
    "because the file reads as protected. Use Read(...) and Edit(...).",
    "",
    "Precedence is deny -> ask -> allow, first match wins, and a deny rule",
    "cannot carry an exception. Rules here override any allow rule a developer",
    "adds in their own settings.local.json."
  ],
